// ═══ Check characteristics of different sources ═══

// ArrayList: ORDERED | SIZED
Spliterator<String> listSplit = List.of("A", "B", "C").spliterator();
// listSplit.characteristics() includes ORDERED and SIZED

// HashSet: SIZED | DISTINCT (NOT ordered!)
Spliterator<String> setSplit = Set.of("A", "B", "C").spliterator();
// DISTINCT: elements are unique. No ORDERED — iteration order undefined.

// TreeSet: ORDERED | SORTED | DISTINCT | SIZED
Spliterator<String> treeSplit = new TreeSet<>(List.of("C", "A", "B")).spliterator();
// SORTED: already sorted. DISTINCT: set guarantees unique. ORDERED: sorted order.

// ═══ HOW PIPELINE USES FLAGS ═══

// 1. SIZED → pre-allocate toList() container:
// ArrayList source (SIZED) → pipeline knows final size → allocates exact ArrayList
// Avoids repeated array resizing during collection.

// 2. SORTED → skip sorted():
// TreeSet source (SORTED) → stream().sorted() is a NO-OP! Already sorted.

// 3. DISTINCT → skip distinct():
// Set source (DISTINCT) → stream().distinct() is a NO-OP! Already unique.

// 4. !ORDERED → forEach unordered in parallel:
// HashSet (not ORDERED) → parallelStream().forEach() can execute in ANY order — faster!
// ArrayList (ORDERED) → parallelStream().forEach() still unordered,
//   but forEachOrdered must coordinate — slower.
